ufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/060.html) ; Tokyo University of Foreign Studies ; No open license verified ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (12 October 2026)\n"},{"id":"japan-adv-iwami-ports","title":"Pourquoi la mine d’Iwami Ginzan inclut-elle des routes et ports ?","domain":"history","level":"culture","aliases":["Iwami Ginzan","石見銀山","argent","ports","commerce"],"explanationFr":"La production d’argent relie extraction, fonte, raffinage, établissements miniers, routes et ports. Le paysage d’Iwami Ginzan conserve ces relations entre montagnes et littoral, d’où les produits circulent notamment vers la Corée et la Chine. Comprendre la mine demande donc de suivre les matériaux et les échanges au-delà du puits d’extraction.","scopeNote":"Cette fiche porte sur les relations documentées dans le bien inscrit, pas sur une estimation de toute la production nationale.","prerequisites":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1246/","title":"Iwami Ginzan Silver Mine","publisher":"UNESCO World Heritage Centre","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","availability":"consulted","license":"Property descriptions display CC-BY-SA IGO 3.0. Photographs, maps and nomination files have separate rights.","reuse":"Original factual synthesis and attribution; no copied description, image, map or audio."}],"backlogRefs":["japan-backlog-history-05","japan-backlog-work-08"],"status":"source-reviewed-draft","claimType":"fact","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","reviewState":{"sourceClaim":"checked","japaneseExample":"not-applicable","nativeReview":"pending"},"examples":[],"levelEstimated":false,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/japan/JapanAdvancedRecords.json","corpus":"japan","recordShard":190,"markdown":"## japan-adv-iwami-ports : Pourquoi la mine d’Iwami Ginzan inclut-elle des routes et ports ? (12 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : history ; niveau : culture ; statut : source-reviewed-draft. (12 October 2026)\n\nLa production d’argent relie extraction, fonte, raffinage, établissements miniers, routes et ports. Le paysage d’Iwami Ginzan conserve ces relations entre montagnes et littoral, d’où les produits circulent notamment vers la Corée et la Chine. Comprendre la mine demande donc de suivre les matériaux et les échanges au-delà du puits d’extraction. (12 October 2026)\n\n- [Iwami Ginzan Silver Mine](https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1246/) ; UNESCO World Heritage Centre ; Property descriptions display CC-BY-SA IGO 3.0. Photographs, maps and nomination files have separate rights. ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (12 October 2026)\n"},{"id":"japan-shoes-home","title":"Quand enlever ses chaussures ?","domain":"daily-life","level":"culture","aliases":["靴","玄関","chaussures","entrée"],"explanationFr":"Dans de nombreux logements, on enlève ses chaussures à l’entrée. Certains restaurants et lieux religieux ont la même règle. Les panneaux et l’indication de l’hôte précisent ce qui est attendu sur place.","examples":[{"ja":"ここで靴を脱ぎますか。","reading":"ここでくつをぬぎますか。","fr":"Dois-je enlever mes chaussures ici ?","provenance":"Original pedagogical example, not a source quotation."}],"prerequisites":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.japan.travel/en/guide/japanese-manners-dos-and-donts/","title":"Japanese Manners Do’s and Don’ts","publisher":"Japan National Tourism Organization","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","license":"No blanket redistribution permission established; factual synthesis and original examples only.","reuse":"Link attribution. No copied article, image, map, or audio."}],"status":"source-reviewed-draft","claimType":"documented-practice","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","reviewState":{"sourceClaim":"checked","japaneseExample":"editorial-draft","nativeReview":"pending"},"scopeNote":"Fiche introductive ; ne prétend pas couvrir tout le thème.","levelEstimated":false,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/japan/JapanCards.json","corpus":"japan","recordShard":190,"markdown":"## japan-shoes-home : Quand enlever ses chaussur